{"causes":["Sun Microsystems was facing financial difficulties and needed to create a new product that could attract investors.","The computing industry was shifting towards the internet and mobile devices, creating an opportunity for a versatile programming language.","The work of various computer scientists and engineers at Sun Microsystems laid the groundwork for Java's development."],"effects":["The widespread adoption of Java led to the creation of numerous popular technologies, including Android operating systems and LinkedIn social networks.","Java became an essential tool for building web applications, mobile devices, and enterprise software.","The language's influence can be seen in the development of numerous other programming languages, including Kotlin and Scala."],"relationships":[{"sourceSlug":"Sun_Microsystems","sourceName":"Sun Microsystems","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"java","targetName":"Java","context":"The company's researchers created the first version of Java in the mid-1990s."},{"sourceSlug":"Mountain_View,_California","sourceName":"Mountain View, California","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"java","targetName":"Java","context":"The language's first public demonstration took place on November 9, 1995, at Sun Microsystems' office in Mountain View."},{"sourceSlug":"Android_Operating_Systems","sourceName":"Android Operating Systems","verb":"CREATES","targetSlug":"java","targetName":"Java","context":"The language's influence can be seen in the development of Android operating systems, which rely heavily on Java."},{"sourceSlug":"Netflix_Streaming_Services","sourceName":"Netflix Streaming Services","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"java","targetName":"Java","context":"The language's versatility makes it an essential tool for building web applications, mobile devices, and enterprise software."},{"sourceSlug":"LinkedIn_Social_Networks","sourceName":"LinkedIn Social Networks","verb":"CREATES","targetSlug":"java","targetName":"Java","context":"The language's influence can be seen in the development of LinkedIn social networks, which rely on Java for their backend functionality."}],"places":[{"name":"Mountain View, California","role":"Development site"},{"name":"United States","role":"Influence region"},{"name":"California","role":"Influence region"}],"texts":[{"title":"Wikipedia: Java","type":"Reference article","slug":"java"}],"externalLinks":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q251","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Java_(programming_language)"],"tags":["software","Computing & Digital Technology","scientific-paradigm"],"thumbnailUrl":"","quote":"","legacySummary":"Java is remembered as a landmark idea of the Contemporary era, referenced in 157 Wikipedia language editions. Key lasting impacts include: Influenced intellectual traditions and cultural development.","summary":"Java is a high-level, general-purpose, object-oriented programming language developed by Sun Microsystems — primarily by James Gosling — with its first public release in 1995. Java was designed around the principle of 'Write Once, Run Anywhere' (WORA): Java source code is compiled to bytecode that runs on the Java Virtual Machine (JVM), an abstract computing machine that can be implemented on any hardware or operating system, making Java programmes inherently portable across platforms. This design philosophy — and Java's combination of object-oriented structure, memory safety (automatic garbage collection), strong typing, and large standard library — made Java one of the most widely adopted programming languages in the world, and it dominated enterprise software development and server-side programming for over two decades.

Java's trajectory after its 1995 release was shaped by several key moments: its adoption for web browser applets (which briefly made Java the primary client-side web technology before being superseded by JavaScript), its use as the primary language for Android mobile application development (announced 2008, which gave Java a second era of massive adoption), its central role in enterprise server-side development through Java EE (now Jakarta EE) and frameworks like Spring and Hibernate, and its acquisition by Oracle through the purchase of Sun Microsystems in 2010. The Oracle acquisition led to the Java vs. Google lawsuit (Oracle v. Google) — a decade-long legal dispute over whether Google's use of Java APIs in Android constituted copyright infringement, ultimately resolved in Google's favour by the US Supreme Court in 2021.

Java's influence on the broader programming ecosystem has been immense: it popularised object-oriented programming and design patterns for a generation of developers, its JVM became the platform for numerous other languages (Kotlin, Scala, Clojure, Groovy), and its ecosystem of tools, frameworks, and libraries set the standard for enterprise software development. By the 2020s, Java had been joined by Kotlin (the preferred Android language since Google's 2017 designation) and Python as dominant general-purpose languages, but remained one of the most widely used languages worldwide.","subjects":["Programming Languages","Computer Science","Contemporary Era","Software Engineering","Technology","Internet History","Object-Oriented Programming","Enterprise Software"],"frameworks":["STRUCTURAL_ANALYSIS","CAUSE_AND_EFFECT","WORLD_SYSTEMS"],"historicalSignificance":{"significanceScore":7,"significanceNarrative":"Java's creation had a significant impact on the tech industry, shaping the development of numerous popular technologies and influencing the way we interact with technology today.","significanceCategory":"regional"},"_editLog":[]}
